d with a rounded tip. Endophallus with long, wavy flagellum, with two spiniform projections — one on each side — at the apex. Spermatheca: Short, sclerotized, and hook-shaped. Cornu is slightly curved, with a rounded apex and obtuse internal angle. Elongated nodulus, slightly wider than cornu; and as wide as the middle part, except the basal region which is narrower. Spermathecal duct is thin and slightly S-shaped.","","text","",""]]},"N892H":{"d":[["General distribution. Endemic species for Iranian fauna.","","text","",""],["Regional distribution. Mazandaran (Hazar Chay, Kazanak; Abu Ask bei Demavand, 1700 m (Elbursgebirge )) (Wittmer 1986).","","text","",""]]},"N8H47":{"d":[["Norway","NO","iso","native",""]]},"NDJJS":{"d":[["North America","","text","",""]]},"NF4Q":{"d":[["Norway","NO","iso","",""]]},"NPQ8R":{"d":[["","BR","iso","native",""],["","CO","iso","native",""]]},"P8JG":{"d":[["California","8977","mrgid","",""],["Temperate Northern Pacific","21725","mrgid","",""]]},"PCT2":{"d":[["","GER","tdwg","",""]]},"RDMTB":{"d":[["Middle America","","text","",""],["North America","","text","",""]]},"RGX62":{"d":[["Distribution. Known from two localities in the extreme south-western part of the Hindukush Mountain Ridge.","","text","",""]]},"RNNSX":{"d":[["Denmark","DK","iso","","not evaluated"]]},"RNNT7":{"d":[["Sweden","SE","iso","native",""]]},"RQ2D":{"d":[["Australasia","","text","native",""]]},"RRFWX":{"d":[["Distribution. Upper Aalenian, Bradfordensis Zone (Gigantea Subzone) to? Lower Bajocian; England, France, Germany, Luxembourg.","","text","",""]]},"RZQJ2":{"d":[["Afrotropic","","text","native",""]]},"S2VTJ":{"d":[["Southern Asia","","text","",""]]},"S3KH":{"d":[["South America","","text","",""]]},"SB7CJ":{"d":[["China","8603","mrgid","native",""]]},"SMKY5":{"d":[["Distribution. R. vadaszii was first described by R ́ asky (1945) from middle Eocene borehole samples (60 m depth) at G ́ ant, in beds roughly equivalent laterally to the outcrop succession studied here. Therefore, the samples studied may be considered topotypes. Subsequently, the age of this variety was suggested to be upper Bartonian by Bignot et al. (1985) based on the associated microfossils (foraminifers, ostracods and pollen) from the same beds of the bauxite cover-sequence at the G ́ ant section (V ́ ertes Hills). R. peckii var. vadaszii has also been well documented in France, in the upper Bartonian of the Paris Basin (Grambast 1957, 1958, 1962 a; Riveline 1986) and from several basins in southern France (Feist-Castel 1976). Anadon & Feist (1981) and Anad ́ on et al. (1992) documented this variety also in the upper Bartonian of the Eastern Ebro Basin (Catalonia, Spain).","","text","",""]]},"SXMSN":{"d":[["Australia","","text","",""]]},"TR7NN":{"d":[["DISTRIBUTION. — At the Mont-des-Récollets it is known from Unit B 4 at the top of the Brussel Sand Formation and in the overlying Lede Sand Formation, up into the base of the Wemmel Sand Member. It rarely occurs elsewhere in the Lede Sand Formation (e. g. recorded at Balegem, Oosterzele, etc.).","","text","",""]]},"V2PTM":{"d":[["Iran","","text","",""]]},"V4JZK":{"d":[["KH","KH","iso","",""],["Môndól Kiri","","text","",""]]},"V4K9K":{"d":[["Distribution Taiwan. Bionomics See the Bionomics section of M. immortalibestia gen. et sp. nov. below.","","text","",""]]},"V55C6":{"d":[["China","","text","",""]]},"VBVWT":{"d":[["Distribution Known only from the type locality in Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region, China.","","text","",""]]},"VBW6T":{"d":[["","CO","iso","",""]]},"VBW73":{"d":[["","CO","iso","",""]]},"VC5WT":{"d":[["New Zealand Exclusive Economic Zone","8455","mrgid","",""]]},"VCDYC":{"d":[["Andes of Peru and western Bolivia","","text","",""]]},"VWXT":{"d":[["Guerrero","18623","mrgid","",""],["Mexico","2224","mrgid","",""]]},"VWY3":{"d":[["Tennessee","19570","mrgid","",""],["Tennessee","19570","mrgid","",""]]},"VX7T":{"d":[["peninsular Malaysia (Terengganu, Perak); Borneo","","text","",""]]},"W6Y3":{"d":[["